---
import ArticleLayout from "@layouts/ArticleLayout.astro";
---

<ArticleLayout
  title="pi-gatekeeper"
  description="A Pi extension that keeps a coding agent working until a verification command passes."
  subtitle="Done means the checks pass."
  eyebrow="2026 · Open source / Developer tools"
  tags="Pi · TypeScript · Verification"
>
  <figure slot="art" class="gatekeeper-art">
    <img
      src="/assets/pi-gatekeeper/card.jpg"
      alt="A robot walking through a glowing green gate marked with a checkmark"
      width="1672"
      height="941"
    />
  </figure>

  <p class="lead">
    Coding agents can make a plausible change and declare victory before the
    tests or typechecker agree. pi-gatekeeper puts a verification step between
    the edit and the finish line.
  </p>
  <a
    class="text-link"
    href="https://github.com/j3hn/pi-gatekeeper"
    target="_blank"
    rel="noopener noreferrer"
  >
    View the repository on GitHub ↗
  </a>

  <section>
    <h2>A feedback loop for finishing</h2>
    <p>
      When Pi is about to finish after a task that may have changed something,
      the extension runs your check command. If it fails, the output is fed back
      to the agent so it can investigate and try again. Repeated identical
      failures prompt a change of approach, and an attempt limit prevents the
      loop from running forever.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Your project, your checks</h2>
    <p>
      Set <code>PI_GATEKEEPER_CHECK</code> to the command you want to run, or
      let the extension find a <code>check</code> script in your package.json.
      If neither is available, the gate stays idle rather than guessing. The
      <code>/gate</code> commands let you check its status or run verification
      yourself.
    </p>
    <p>
      An optional rollback can restore tracked files to their pre-task state
      after repeated failures. It is off by default: rollback can also undo
      manual edits, and it does not remove untracked files.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Try it with Pi</h2>
    <p>
      Install the extension from npm, then choose a non-interactive check that
      suits your project.
    </p>
    <pre><code>pi install npm:pi-gatekeeper</code></pre>
    <a
      class="text-link"
      href="https://github.com/j3hn/pi-gatekeeper#readme"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
    >
      Setup and configuration on GitHub ↗
    </a>
  </section>
</ArticleLayout>

<style>
  .gatekeeper-art {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .gatekeeper-art img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
</style>
